Description: Window ▸ Always on Top: keep a floating window above the others
 niri stacks floating windows by when they were last raised and cannot pin
 one. This adds the IPC action `set-window-always-on-top --id N --on true`
 (`niri msg action set-window-always-on-top`, no key bind) and
 `Window.is_always_on_top` on the IPC window, which the event stream
 re-sends when it changes. In the floating layout, pinned windows keep the
 front of the stack in pinning order: opening or activating any other
 window raises it only as far as the first window that is not pinned. A
 tiled window is made floating first. Lulo OS's menu bar uses it for
 Calculator's Window ▸ Always on Top (CALC-08).
 .
 See docs/decisions/0031-niri-always-on-top.md in the rmac repository.
Author: Jacob Samas <samasjacob@icloud.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
